  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch15-08> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch15-08--gpt> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch15-08--gpt> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "GPT-5.6 Sol on thompson1917-ch15-08: resolvable-now, resolvability 0.81" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.809"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "resolvable-now" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.92"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "The assertion that S. mansoni is not a separate species has a decisive test using abundant modern genomic data. The specific funnel-moulding mechanism is less well covered, but the compound claim can be clearly refuted or supported at its principal taxonomic consequence." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Link egg spine position to independently identified adult worms using morphology and genomic sequences, and test whether lateral- and terminal-spined eggs occur within one reproducing lineage or segregate into distinct lineages. Stable genomic separation supports separate species and refutes Thompson; within-lineage mechanical switching would support his claim." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Historical egg images may not be linked to sequenced adult worms.", "Hybridization can complicate species boundaries.", "Public data test species distinctness more directly than ootype moulding." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/thompson1917-ch15-08--gpt--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/thompson1917-ch15-08--gpt--dataset-2>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/thompson1917-ch15-08--gpt--dataset-3> .
